      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think everyone using quest headsets is getting this issue.  Doing the VRC sound test, there is hardly any movement on the spectrum analyzer in game.  You have to have the mic cranked to maximum in Virtual Desktop to get sound to work or people can't hear you.  This then messes up the threshold, having it anything above 3 percent, people can't hear you.  Below that, people are getting audio feedback from the speakers.  Please fix.  It only does this on VRC.  No issues on other platforms.  I can confirm it's happening with at least three other people I regularly talk to. It's hard to describe exactly and very annoying.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
